# Without this file, core.autocrlf decides line endings per checkout, so the
# same commit yields different bytes on Windows and Linux. That is fine for
# compilation and fatal for a checksum baseline: the burden-paper regression
# test hashes these files, and it would fail on a fresh Windows clone for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the analysis.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Build outputs and data that must survive byte-for-byte.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db    binary
